nspire_file_read: never copy past the caller's buffer

The read loop copied every chunk the calculator sent, even once the
buffer passed in was full, so a file larger than "size" overflowed it.
Some files change size between reads (NspireLogs.zip is generated on
each read), so callers cannot guarantee the size in advance. Stop
copying when the buffer is full; *total_bytes still reports the full
length so the caller can retry with a larger buffer.

diff --git a/src/services/file.c b/src/services/file.c
index d1250b1..0883524 100644
--- a/src/services/file.c
+++ b/src/services/file.c
@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@ int nspire_file_read(nspire_handle_t *handle, const char *path,
 
 		if (size) {
 			size_t to_copy = len - 1;
+			if (to_copy > size)
+				to_copy = size;
 			memcpy(ptr, buffer + 1, to_copy);
 			size -= to_copy;
 
